    "updated_at": "2026-04-13T15:43:54Z",
    "body": "It seems that the [post-connection steps are sync, while the removing steps queue a microtask](https://whatpr.org/html/12263/107f8ed...86b46b3/form-elements.html#:~:text=insertedOption%20%2E-,The,removedNode%20%2E). I think it would be more consistent if both were queueing a microtask?\r\n\r\nAlso -- I think that [reset](https://whatpr.org/html/12263/107f8ed...86b46b3/form-elements.html#selectedness-setting-algorithm:~:text=Run%20the%20selectedness%20setting%20algorithm%20given%20selectElement%20%2E%20and%20false%2E) would now also run script because it clones into selectedcontent, which I think it shouldn't (at least in Gecko it is marked as not script running). Should we also queue a microtask here?",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/4237631967/reactions",
