    "updated_at": "2026-06-24T09:29:25Z",
    "body": "I think the flakiness you can get is that depending on when the parser yields and the microtask runs, the contents of the `option` element might have changed, or in case of `selectedcontent` element callbacks, the currently selected `option` element might have changed.\r\n\r\nOne thing we could consider doing still I think is doing the clone synchronously, but the insertion asynchronously, but that still leaves us with the problem of running the clone for the `option` element too early as we want to clone when we see the end tag, not when we've only seen the start tag.",
